<article class="env-example" id="0BWI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BWI">Example <span data-tag="0BWI">49.12.5</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $f, h \in A[x]$ such that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  B = (A[x]/(f))_ h = A[x, 1/h]/(f)  \]
</div>
  <p> is quasi-finite over $A$. Let $f' \in A[x]$ be the derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$. The ideal $\mathfrak {D} = (f') \subset B$ is the Noether different of $B$ over $A$, is the Kähler different of $B$ over $A$, and is the ideal whose associated quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals is the different of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B)$ over $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$. </p>
</article>